  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certifies that the matter described above is lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reasons:\r\n\r\nThe proposed roof extension comprising a rear dormer with dimensions of 3.8m deep, 2.5m high and 4.5m wide, equating to a volume of 21.38m3, together with the existing rear extension and glasshouse, which have a combined volume of volume of 21.73m3, brings the total extension volume of the original dwellinghouse to 43.11m3 and qualifies as Class B permitted development within Part 1 of Schedule 2 of The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995.  It does not therefore require planning permission."
